# MonkeyLM Agent Context File
# This file defines the architectural standards and patterns enforced in this repository.
# Future AI agents MUST read this file before making any modifications.

## Structural Transformations Performed

### 1. Type Extraction (monkeylm/types.py)
- All dataclasses (Settings, PageSnapshot, FormControlRecord, DefectTicket, etc.) extracted from config.py
- Zero runtime logic or I/O in types.py — pure data definitions only
- Enables circular-import-free access from any module

### 2. Error Hierarchy (monkeylm/errors.py)
- Centralized exception hierarchy rooted at `MonkeyLMError`
- Typed subclasses: ConfigurationError, BrowserError, ModelError, PersistenceError, NavigationError, ValidationError, ShutdownRequested
- All carry structured context (url, selector, model, service) for logging

### 3. Shutdown Handler Consolidation
- `_request_graceful_shutdown` and `_register_graceful_shutdown_signals` live ONLY in config.py
- Duplicate implementations removed from core.py

### 4. Dead Code Removal
- `monkey_agent_advanced.py` (799-line backward-compat shim) — removed
- `test.py` (292-line standalone script duplicating engine) — removed

### 5. Import Standardization
- All modules use `from monkeylm.types import ...` for dataclasses
- All modules use `from monkeylm.config import ...` for config/helpers
- All modules have explicit `__all__` exports

## Enforced Architectural Paradigms

### Module Layout
```
monkeylm/
  __init__.py     # Public API re-exports only
  __main__.py     # Entry point
  config.py       # Settings, CLI, env loading, helpers
  types.py        # All dataclasses and type definitions
  errors.py       # Centralized exception hierarchy
  memory.py       # PostgreSQL, Redis, Qdrant persistence
  models.py       # LLM client, prompts, vision routing
  browser.py      # Playwright lifecycle, DOM, actions
  reporting.py    # Markdown, JSON, PDF, HTML reports
  core.py         # Main loop, workers, monitor classes
  resources/      # Bundled third-party assets
```

### Typing & Structure
- All functions MUST have type annotations
- All modules MUST have `from __future__ import annotations`
- All modules MUST have `__all__` with explicit export list
- Dataclasses go in types.py, NOT config.py

### Error Handling
- Catch `MonkeyLMError` for all application-specific errors
- Use typed subclasses (BrowserError, ModelError, etc.) for granular handling
- Never use bare `except Exception` without logging

### Agent Interoperability
- No global mutable state across module boundaries
- No backward-compat shims or wrapper classes
- No conversational AI comments ("FIX (Layer 1)", "GUARDRAIL (Layer 2)")
- Docstrings are concise, structured, and programmatically valid

### Dependency Management
- All dependencies strictly pinned in requirements.txt
- Optional imports use `_optional_import()` pattern from config.py
- No runtime network fetches for bundled assets (axe-core is local)

## System Instruction Prompt for Future Agents

```
You are working on the MonkeyLM codebase. Before making any changes:

1. Read .agentrules to understand the enforced architecture.
2. All dataclasses live in monkeylm/types.py — never add new dataclasses to config.py.
3. All custom exceptions inherit from monkeylm.errors.MonkeyLMError.
4. Every module must have `from __future__ import annotations`, type annotations, and `__all__`.
5. No backward-compat shims, wrapper classes, or mutable global state across modules.
6. No conversational AI comments — use concise, structured docstrings only.
7. Run `ruff check monkeylm/ tests/` before committing.
8. Run `pytest tests/` to verify all tests pass.
```
